## 3. Stage-by-Stage Mint-to Logic™ & Shepherd's Process Analysis

* **`[100]` Intake & Sensor/Command Boundary Normalization:** Ingests physical telemetry, PLC/controller signals, and control commands across IT/OT boundaries—echoing multi-source intake/triggers while operating on industrial protocols and physical sensors rather than a universal Mint Unit intake bus.
* **`[200]` Validation / Safety Interlock, Firmware & Threshold Checks:** Validates commands and process states against physical safety envelopes, signed/validated SIS logic, and firmware integrity baselines before actuation.
* **`[300]` Mint Unit / Process State & Control Context:** Tracks controller/loop state, equipment mode, and sequence/batch context, without minting a standalone cryptographic Mint Unit Container with routing directives and commit finalization.
* **`[400]` Routing / Control Loop Dispatch & Zone/Conduit Routing:** Routes control actions and telemetry across segmented zones and conduits—mirroring structured routing without branching a discrete unit into Burn, Limbo, Access, or Code states.
* **`[500a]` Burn / Safe-State Trip, Lockout & Credential/Session Termination:** Triggers fail-safe trips, operator lockouts, or session/connection teardown to prevent physical harm—paralleling decisive termination/containment rather than an authorization-gated single-use credential burn on a discrete mint unit.
* **`[500b]` Limbo / Safe Hold, Fallback Mode & Interlock Hold:** Holds operations in safe/manual/degraded fallback states when conditions exceed bounds or drift from safe envelopes—showing strong operational alignment with The Shepherd's Method™ / Process around continuous safety pacing and controlled holds.
* **`[500c]` Access / Zone-and-Conduit Segmentation, Data Diodes & SIS Isolation:** Enforces strict physical/logical isolation across zones, conduits, data diodes, and independent SIS hardware/logic—one of the strongest real-world parallels to hard boundary containment.
* **`[500d]` Code / PLC/Actuator Execution & Physical Process Coupling:** Executes control logic on PLCs, actuators, and physical plants where software decisions have immediate physical consequences—requiring strict pre-actuation safety assurance.
* **`[600]` Audit / OT Event Logs, Forensic Readiness & Safety Records:** Captures controller events, safety trips, configuration changes, and forensic telemetry—supporting post-incident investigation and regulatory/safety compliance.

